### Page 1 of 2

```text
RESOLUTION NO. __________

ENTITLED: "A RESOLUTION EXPRESSING THE APPRECIATION OF THE
GOVERNING BODY FOR THE WORK OF DIRECTOR NEMECEK,
DIRECTOR SANCHEZ, AND THEIR RESPECTIVE DEPARTMENTS, ON
CORRECTING DEFICIENCIES AND IMPROVING AND MAINTAINING
CERTAIN
EXTERIOR
COMPONENTS
OF
THE
MUNICIPAL
BUILDING."

WHEREAS, on March 23, 2024, a Resolution was introduced for consideration by the
Governing Body, which required the submittal of a report by the Public Works Department
analyzing the best avenue for correcting certain deficiencies and improving and maintaining the
west entryway to the Municipal Building;

WHEREAS, the deficiencies and areas for improvement identified in the Resolution
included necessary maintenance on exterior soffits and bricks and portions of the exterior
pavement around the main entrance which were failing. The Resolution further noted security
concerns regarding the ingress and egress from the main entrance due to the age and current state
of the doors at the entryway and needed improvements to the building's landscaping around the
main entrance;

WHEREAS, upon introduction, the Resolution was referred to the Public Services
Committee for further consideration. At the April 2, 2024, committee meeting, Vicki Nemecek,
Director of the Public Works Department, testified to the issues identified in the Resolution;

WHEREAS, Director Nemecek stated that her department was taking affirmative action in
response to the concerns raised in the Resolution, including plans to paint rusted soffits,
coordination with an appropriate architectural firm to address the needed maintenance on the
failing exterior brick and obtaining a quote for related work on brick suffering from efflorescence;

WHEREAS, regarding the failing exterior pavement, Director Nemecek stated that this
concern was to be addressed as part of the department's Public Works Improvement Project, which
will address deteriorating concrete and asphalt at several Public Works city facilities. Director
Nemecek further stated that the project design had been finalized and once bid, the pavement issues
around the main entrance should be addressed by late summer or fall of 2024;

WHEREAS, regarding the concerns surrounding the doors at the main entryway, Director
Nemecek stated work had already begun to remove and replace the faulty doors;

WHEREAS, regarding the needed improvements to the building's landscaping, Director
Nemecek stated she was coordinating with Jason Sanchez, Director of the Community Recreation
and Events Department, to address and remediate both the building's landscaping and irrigation
system. She noted that a complete remediation would require a significant financial investment,
but Director Sanchez stated his department would work, within budgetary constraints, to improve
the problem areas; and

1:20 pm, Jun 05, 2024
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
Page 2 of 2
WHEREAS, based on the testimony provided at the Public Services Committee, the
committee members voted not to advance further consideration of the Resolution because city staff
had adequately responded to the concerns stated therein.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY
OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that the Governing Body appreciates the due attention given by
Director Nemecek, Director Sanchez, and their respective departments, to the concerns raised by
the Resolution;

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that the Governing Body appreciates the urgency with
which Director Nemecek, Director Sanchez, and their respective departments, treated these
concerns and their work conducted to address the concerns in a meaningful way; and

BE IT  FINALY RESOLVED, that the Governing Body seeks to more formally recognize
Director Nemecek, Director Sanchez, and their respective departments, through the adoption of
the present Resolution to thank everyone for their continued work on the municipal building,
consistent with the previously identified concerns, to enhance and maintain public perception and
experience.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED this _______ day of _____________________,
2024.

__________________________________________
Patrick Collins, Mayor

(SEAL)

ATTEST:

____________________________________
Kristina F. Jones, City Clerk
